.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-server-agent-get - Guest agent version


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro server agent get  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Guest agent version

.PP
The Gyro guest agent configures private network cards and the public-IP-off route inside the server. Servers installed before 14 November 2026 run an older agent: a card attaches but \fBapplied\fR stays false and turning the public IP off answers 409 \fBagent_update_required\fR\&. \fBupdate_command\fR is a one-line command to run on the server as root (downloads Gyro's versioned updater and checks its SHA-256); it only replaces the agent, needs no restart and does not touch your data. If you gave the card an address yourself (netplan), delete that file and run \fBnetplan apply\fR afterwards. The version is read from the server when it is running.

.PP
API: GET /cloud/servers/{id}/agent (operationId getServerAgent, scope cloud_read)


